	(text "Two host ports. USB-C is a 20 Gbit/s device (FX20), the way a HackRF is a peripheral. QSFP-DD is 400GbE, because a 10 GHz instantaneous bandwidth at 12-bit complex is about 240 Gbit/s and does not fit in USB. FX20 LVDS is FPGA-to-host only. Host-to-FPGA samples on USB use the 32-bit LVCMOS bus at about 5 Gbit/s."
		(at 20.00 18.00 0)
		(effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)))
		(uuid "827ef25b-21b8-55f9-af16-e08de43173b5")
	)
